#: src/toyota_telemetry/ui/shell.py:476
msgid "Endpoint: one diagnostic route to an ECU (tester and response CAN IDs plus a reviewed session). Confirmed endpoints are recorded in the project; others are candidates until they respond."
msgstr ""

#: src/toyota_telemetry/ui/shell.py:478
msgid "DID: one data request on an endpoint. A DID can carry several signals, so its interval is shared."
msgstr ""

#: src/toyota_telemetry/ui/shell.py:479
msgid "Signal: one interpreted value inside a DID response; it is what you review, target, and plot."
msgstr ""

#: src/toyota_telemetry/ui/shell.py:480
msgid "Target: the evidence still wanted for a signal, such as minimum samples or required states. A transition is any change of raw value; a change counts only when the decoded value moves by at least the minimum difference."
msgstr ""

#: src/toyota_telemetry/ui/shell.py:483
msgid "Signal status: Not checked, then Responds (its DID answered), Recorded (samples saved), and Reviewed (its meaning confirmed). Refused means the ECU rejected the request. No answer means its ECU did not answer when verified, so it was not read; verifying again later (for example with the engine running) may reach it."
msgstr ""

#: src/toyota_telemetry/ui/shell.py:487
msgid "Diagnostic session: the mode an ECU is switched to before it is read. Most ECUs answer more requests in the extended session (request 10 03) than in the default one. The choices are the session steps reviewed in the project's transport settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/toyota_telemetry/ui/shell.py:490
msgid "Verify vs Confirm endpoint: Verify transmits read requests to see which DIDs answer. Confirm endpoint transmits nothing; it records your review that an endpoint which answered is the ECU you think it is, with where the evidence is written up. Collection needs both."
msgstr ""

#: src/toyota_telemetry/ui/shell.py:493
msgid "Refusal codes: when an ECU rejects a request it returns a code, e.g. 0x31 (request out of range) or 0x22 (conditions not correct); the app names common ones."
msgstr ""

#: src/toyota_telemetry/ui/shell.py:495
msgid "Run: one recording session, saved as one folder. Delete moves a run's folder to the system trash; restore it from there to bring the run back."
msgstr ""

#: src/toyota_telemetry/ui/shell.py:497
msgid "Interrupted run: a recording that stopped without finishing. Recover keeps everything saved up to the interruption."
msgstr ""

#: src/toyota_telemetry/ui/shell.py:499
msgid "Only actions with a warning icon (Verify, Live view, and Start) transmit to the vehicle, and each shows its exact scope first. Live view reads one DID at its collection interval and shows the values without recording them; Pause stops sending."
msgstr ""

